    "narrative": "With the schedule thin today, the Austin Waves are looking for efficiency from a condensed roster. **Liam Hicks** holds the highest mark on the board at 55.93. While his status remains listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" the assumption that he hits cleanup against Shawn Armstrong provides the most stable path to counting stats today. His score is bolstered by a favorable 4.35 xERA matchup and a dynamic platoon advantage (+11%) that positions him as our primary offensive anchor. Conversely, **Brayan Rocchio** sits at a 49.70, teetering on the edge of the marginal threshold. His utility is suppressed by his projected ninth-spot in the order, which effectively caps his run-production ceiling despite a decent matchup against Nick Martinez.\n\nThe bench remains largely quiet today due to league-wide scheduling, but the absence of our core producers\u2014**Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**\u2014highlights the difficulty of navigating a light day. Among the rest of our depth, including **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara**, none were viable starts given the lack of game action. The most pressing roster concern remains **Luis Robert Jr.**, who is currently sidelined on the IL; his recovery is critical for our pursuit of stolen bases, as his absence continues to force us to rely on marginal floor plays like **Brayan Rocchio** to fill the gaps. Keep a close watch on the official lineups for **Liam Hicks** and **Brayan Rocchio**, as any deviation from these assumed batting slots will necessitate an immediate reassessment of our daily efficiency output.",
